2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO] V2.5.20 [2026-08-31] STALE-DATA GUARD THRESHOLD 16 -> 20 MIN (15m + fut15).
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]   WHAT : in the V2.5.15 stale-data guard, _fresh_limit = now - 16min becomes
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          now - _stale_max_min (20). The [STALE] log line now prints the
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          constant instead of a hardcoded ">16min". NO entry/exit RULE, no
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          engine, no indicator touched -- this only changes when the guard
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          declares the frame unusable and blocks entries for one cycle.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]   WHY  : a bar's LABEL is its bucket START, so a perfectly current 15m bar is
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          already 15 min old by label the instant the next bucket opens. 16 min
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          left only ~60s of headroom, and the tick samples the new bucket a few
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          seconds BEFORE its first 1m candle exists, so the shim (correctly) has
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          no bar to build yet and returns the previous bucket. The guard then
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          fired once per bucket, always at :01/:16/:31/:46, always recovering on
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          the very next tick. This is a threshold artefact, NOT stale data.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,563 [INFO]          Supersedes the 08-29 note "Deliberately NOT raising the 16-min stale
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          guard": that reasoning assumed the shim would make the forming bar
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          available immediately, which it cannot do inside the first ~60s of a
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          bucket. 20 = 15 (bar width) + 5 (publish/tick tolerance).
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]   EVIDENCE: 2026-08-31 live logs, first full day on the resampling shim.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          Nifty 18 [STALE] events, Sensex 18 -- each one blocking entries for a
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          cycle. Replayed every one of the 36 against the recorded tick time and
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          bar label: bar-label age ranged 16.00-16.45 min, i.e. ALL 36 sat
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          inside a 0.45-min band just past the old line. Under 20 min: 0 of 36
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          trip. Margin to the new line is 3.55 min.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          The failure this guard exists for is untouched: the 2026-06-12
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          incident served bars HOURS in the past (13:30 PE entry into a +68pt
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          rally, HARDSL) and is still caught by a wide margin.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]   DIAGNOSIS NOTE: the shim itself was verified NOT to be at fault -- a live
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          probe at 14:02:04 IST on 08-31 returned the 14:00 15m bar (fresh) and
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          1m candles through 14:01, resampling correctly. The bug was only ever
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          the guard's threshold.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]   SECOND, DEPENDENT CHANGE -- _completed_idx() (REQUIRED, not optional):
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          raising the threshold ALONE would have been a net regression, and the
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          08-29 note "raising the guard is the WRONG FIX" was right about why.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          The engines read df15['K'].iloc[-2] (and df1h iloc[-2]) assuming
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          iloc[-1] is ALWAYS the forming bar. In the boundary window it is not,
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          so simply unblocking those cycles would have had the engines evaluate
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          a K one bar (15 min) STALE -- silently. Measured: the guard's instant
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          refetch, 28ms later, recovered 0 of 18 trips, confirming the forming
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          bar is genuinely absent, not merely slow.
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          New module-level _completed_idx(df, now, minutes) returns the offset of
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          the last COMPLETED bar: -2 when the forming bar is present, -1 in the
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          boundary window. Wired into the 2 K/1h read sites (main tick + the
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          guard's recovery branch). The boot-time read at the "Live state + first
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          pulse" block is left on -2 deliberately (one-shot, pre-market-loop).
2026-09-09 03:32:06,564 [INFO]          SAFETY PROPERTY: it returns -2 on every tick that today reaches the
2026-09-09 03:32:06,565 [INFO]          engines, so it CANNOT change any tick that currently produces a trade;
2026-09-09 03:32:06,565 [INFO]          it only differs inside the window that today is unconditionally
2026-09-09 03:32:06,565 [INFO]          blocked. Unit-tested 8 cases + a 96-tick sweep: 0 normal ticks return
2026-09-09 03:32:06,565 [INFO]          anything but -2.
